# The six gem frames on one strip, 32x32 each, drawn at 2x.
#
# Frame 0 is deliberately empty so the sheet can be indexed by Board.Gem
# directly — Gem.Empty is 0, and a lookup table that needs an offset is a
# lookup table someone will eventually get wrong.
#
# Every gem is a different *shape* as well as a different hue. Colour alone
# fails for red/green colour blindness — roughly 8% of players, and red and
# green are exactly the two that will sit next to each other — so shape is the
# redundant channel. It costs nothing here and makes the board playable.
#
# Two steps each, body and highlight, with the highlight always in the same
# upper-left quadrant. Forty shaded spheres would read as noise; forty flat
# tokens with one consistent glint read as a board.
name puzzle-gems
size 192 32
key o outline
key b gem-red
key B gem-red-lite
key c gem-green
key C gem-green-lite
key d gem-cyan
key D gem-cyan-lite
key e gem-yellow
key E gem-yellow-lite
key f gem-violet
key F gem-violet-lite
pixels
